  "id": "d282707c-ec9b-5388-9026-8e28145e8aa1",
  "slug": "homemade-ricotta-gnocchi-recipe-11917522",
  "name": "Homemade Ricotta Gnocchi",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "Have a craving for gnocchi? These homemade ricotta gnocchi are easy to make and are delicious served with your favorite pasta sauce.",
  "cuisine": "Italian",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Scoop flour into a pile on a clean table. Form a well in the center using a fork."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Pour Parmesan, eggs, whole milk ricotta, part-skim ricotta, melted butter, salt, and pepper into the well."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Using the fork, slowly incorporate dry ingredients into wet ingredients, pulling the rim of the well into the center. Once dough begins to form a ball, knead it until the dough comes together and is evenly combined, 2 to 3 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Place dough ball on a large plate; cover with plastic wrap to prevent dough from drying out as you work with it."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Dust a clean surface with flour, then trim off about 1/4 of the dough. Roll this portion into a long round cylinder, about 1-inch in diameter. Slice this strip into 1-inch gnocchi. Repeat this process to shape and cut all of the dough into gnocchi."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Lightly flour a sheet pan. Roll each gnocchi over a microplane or the side of a box grater to add texture to the exterior. Place gnocchi on the sheet pan."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil. Add gnocchi, being careful not to overcrowd the pot. Bring water back to a boil and cook until gnocchi begins to float and the pieces have reached your desired texture, 3 to 5 minutes. Top with your favorite sauce and Parmesan."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 10,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 5,
